# ADVANCED-EDITION-CODE: in the advanced edition's build, never the standard one's.
#
# The advanced settings window's own sources: what its build compiles after every source
# gui/window.sources names, one repository-relative path per line, in the order csc is given
# them, under the one group `[advanced]`.
#
# The standard window is gui/window.sources and nothing else, and its build never reads this
# file, so a type declared in a source listed here cannot reach the standard executable. No
# source of the standard window names one either (advanced/tests/test_advanced_package.py).
#
# The Dashboard's Advanced features page, which joins the standard window through the `partial void`
# points gui/Dashboard.cs declares (DashboardBuilt, SnapshotApplied), its Keep it on and Send now cards
# (v0.6.14), and the page's own audit.

[advanced]
advanced/gui/AdvancedPage.cs
advanced/gui/AdvancedKeepOn.cs
advanced/gui/AdvancedPageAudit.cs
